.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 0 = 3\\).\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 5 = 11\\)  .\n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the hundreds place.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the thousands place.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the ten-thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 7\\).\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 0 = 6\\).\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 0 = 2\\).\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 7 = 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the hundred-millions place.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 8 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the billions place.\n\n10. **Billions place:**  .\n    \\(0 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 1\\).\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:.\n\n\\[", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1392677013'}  1%|1         | 7/500 [00:38<45:08,  5.49s/it]
