ce:**  \n   \\(5 + 7 = 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(1 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  \n   Write down **1** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  \n   \\(9 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 13\\)  \n   Write down **3** and carry over **1**.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  \n   \\(5 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 6\\)  \n   Write down **6**.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:\n\n```\n    591,525,997\n  + 397,622,729\n  ==============\n    989,148,726\n```\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{989,\\!148,\\!726}\\).", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': '\nFirst, I will align the two numbers vertically to ensure that each digit is in the correct place value.\n\nNext, I will add the digits starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and move to the left.\n\nIf the sum of any two digits is 10 or more, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will continue this process for each digit, ensuring that all place values are correctly added and any necessary carrying is accounted for.\n\nFinally, after adding all the digits, I will arrive at the total sum of the two numbers.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '989148726', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': '\nFirst, I will align the two numbers vertically to ensure that each digit is in the correct place value.\n\nNext, I will add the digits starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and move to the left.\n\nIf the sum of any two digits is 10 or more, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will continue this process for each digit, ensuring that all place values are correctly added and any necessary carrying is accounted for.\n\nFinally, after adding all the digits, I will arrive at the total sum of the two numbers.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 591,525,997 and 397,622,729?.\n\n#