dd the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 3 = 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the tens place.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 2 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 9\\)  .\n   Write down **9**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 9 = 11\\)  .\n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the thousands place.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1** to the ten-thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 2 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  .\n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the hundred-thousands place.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the millions place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 8\\)  .\n   Write down **8**.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 8 = 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1** to the hundred-millions place.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 1\\)  .\n   Write down **1**.\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:.\n\n\\[", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1358029192'}
