rry) \\(= 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  \n   \\(8 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 15\\)  \n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(7 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 17\\)  \n   Write down **7** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  \n   \\(3 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  \n   \\(6 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  \n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n10. **Billions place:**  \n    \\(0 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 1\\)\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:\n\n# Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1,434,523,065}\n\\]", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': '\nFirst, I will align the two numbers by their place values to ensure accurate addition.\n\nNext, I will add the digits starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and move to the left.\n\nIf the sum of any two digits exceeds 9, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will continue this process for each place value until all digits have been added.\n\nFinally, I will compile the results to obtain the final sum.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '1434523065', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': '\nFirst, I will align the two numbers by their place values to ensure accurate addition.\n\nNext, I will add the digits starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and move to the left.\n\nIf the sum of any two digits exceeds 9, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will continue this process for each place value until all digits have been added.\n\nFinally, I will compile the results to obtain the final sum.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of **637,836,865** and **796,686,200**?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n```.\n    637,836,865.\n  + 796,686,200.\n  ==============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 0 = 5\\).\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 0 = 6\\).\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 2 = 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 8 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 15\\)  .\n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 17\\)  .\n   Write down **7** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n10. **Billions place:**  .\n    \\(0 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 1\\).\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:.\n\n# Answer:.\n\\[", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1434523965'}  7%|7         | 35/500 [03:24<47:25,  6.12s/it]
