4275920', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 178,826,447 and 975,449,473.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 7 + 3 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 4 + 7 plus the carried over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 4 + 4 plus the carried over 1 equals 9. I'll write down 9.\n\nIn the thousands place: 6 + 9 equals 15. I'll write down 5 and carry over 1 to the ten thousands place.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 2 + 4 plus the carried over 1 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 8 + 5 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 7 + 7 plus the carried over 1 equals 15. I'll write down 5 and carry over 1 to the ten millions place.\n\nIn the ten millions place: 1 + 9 plus the carried over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the hundred millions place.\n\nFinally, in the hundred millions place: 1 + 0 plus the carried over 1 equals 2. I'll write down 2", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 178,826,447 and 975,449,473?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(7 + 3 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the tens place.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(4 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the hundreds place.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(4 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 9\\)  \n   Write down **9**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(6 + 9 = 15\\)  \n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the ten thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  \n   \\(2 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 7\\)  \n   Write down **7**.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  \n   \\(8 + 5 = 13\\)  \n   Write down **3** and carry over **1** to the millions place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(7 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 15\\)  \n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the ten millions place.\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  \n   \\(1 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  \n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the hundred millions place.\n\n9. **Hundred millions place:**  \n   \\(1 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 2\\)  \n   Write down **2**.\n\nCombining all the digits, the final sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1,\\!154,\\!275,\\!920}\n\\]", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1154279920'} 10%|#         | 51/500 [05:00<45:06,  6.03s/it]
