ried over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, in the hundred millions place: 3 + 9 plus the carried over 1 equals 13", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 384,094,105 and 957,165,270?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 0 = 5\\).\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 7 = 7\\).\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(1 + 2 = 3\\).\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 5 = 9\\).\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 6 = 15\\)  .\n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the next higher place.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 7 + 1\\) (carried over) \\(= 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the next higher place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 5 + 1\\) (carried over) \\(= 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the next higher place.\n\n8. **Hundred millions place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 9 + 1\\) (carried over) \\(= 13\\)  .\n   Write down **13**.\n\nCombining all the results from each place:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{0}384,094,105 \\\\.\n+\\,957,165,270 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n1,341,259,375 \\\\.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1341259875'} 16%|#5        | 78/500 [07:38<41:07,  5.85s/it]
