ace.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 9\\).\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 9 = 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 2 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  .\n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 8\\).\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 9 = 11\\)  .\n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 16\\)  .\n   Write down **6** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n10. **Billions place:**  .\n    \\(0 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 1\\).\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:.\n\n\\[", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1594073905'} 16%|#6        | 81/500 [07:57<42:53,  6.14s/it]
