1 (carry over)\n     -------\n       14 (write down 4, carry over 1)\n```\n\n```\n       2 (thousands place)\n     + 2 (thousands place)\n     + 1 (carry over)\n     -------\n       5 (write down 5)\n```\n\n```\n       4 (ten thousands place)\n     + 6 (ten thousands place)\n     -------\n       10 (write down 0, carry over 1)\n```\n\n```\n       2 (hundred thousands place)\n     + 5 (hundred thousands place)\n     + 1 (carry over)\n     -------\n       8 (write down 8)\n```\n\n```\n       7 (millions place)\n     + 4 (millions place)\n     -------\n       11 (write down 1, carry over 1)\n```\n\n```\n       2 (ten millions place)\n     + 6 (ten millions place)\n     + 1 (carry over)\n     -------\n       9 (write down 9)\n```\n\n5. **Combine all the results:**\n\n```\n  276,242,649\n+ 644,562,764\n--------------\n  920,805,413\n```\n\n# Answer:\n\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\boxed{920805413}.", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 276,242,649 and 644,562,764.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the ones place: 9 plus 4 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nThen, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 4 plus 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nI'll continue this process for each subsequent place value, carrying over any excess as needed.\n\nAfter adding all the digits, I'll arrive at the final sum.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '920805413', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 276,242,649 and 644,562,764.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the ones place: 9 plus 4 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nThen, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 4 plus 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nI'll continue this process for each subsequent place value, carrying over any excess as needed.\n\nAfter adding all the digits, I'll arrive at the final sum.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 276,242,649 and 644,562,764?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n1. **Align the numbers by their place values:**.\n\n```.\n  276,242,649.\n+ 644,562,764.\n--------------.\n```.\n\n2. **Add the digits starting from the rightmost digit (ones place):**.\n\n```.\n       9 (ones place).\n     + 4 (ones place).\n     -------.\n       13 (write down 3, carry over 1).\n```.\n\n3. **Move to the tens place:**.\n\n```.\n       4 (tens place).\n     + 6 (tens place).\n     + 1 (carry over).\n     -------.\n       11 (write down 1, carry over 1).\n```.\n\n4. **Continue this process for each subsequent place value:**.\n\n```.\n       6 (hundreds place).\n     + 7 (hundreds place).\n     + 1 (carry over).\n     -------.\n       14 (write down 4, carry over 1).\n```.\n\n```.\n       2 (thousands place).\n     + 2 (thousands place).\n     + 1 (carry over).\n     -------.\n       5 (write down 5).\n```.\n\n```.\n       4 (ten thousands place).\n     + 6 (ten thousands place).\n     -------.\n       10 (write down 0, carry over 1).\n```.\n\n```.\n       2 (hundred thousands place).\n     + 5 (hundred thousands place).\n     + 1 (carry over).\n     -------.\n       8 (write down 8).\n```.\n\n```.\n       7 (millions place).\n     + 4 (millions place).\n     -------.\n       11 (write down 1, carry over 1).\n```.\n\n```.\n       2 (ten millions place).\n     + 6 (ten millions place).\n     + 1 (carry over).\n     -------.\n       9 (write down 9).\n```.\n\n5. **Combine all the results:**.\n\n```.\n  276,242,649.\n+ 644,562,764.\n--------------.\n  920,805,413.\n```.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '920805493'} 18%|#7        | 89/500 [08:46<41:10,  6.01s/it]
