ands place: 4 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 1 + 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 5.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 2 + 8 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, in the hundred millions place: 3 + 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 372,148,610 and 883,994,985?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(0 + 5 = 5\\)\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(1 + 8 = 9\\)\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(6 + 9 = 15\\)  \n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(8 + 4 + 1\\) (carried over) \\(= 13\\)  \n   Write down **3** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  \n   \\(4 + 9 + 1\\) (carried over) \\(= 14\\)  \n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  \n   \\(1 + 3 + 1\\) (carried over) \\(= 5\\)\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(2 + 8 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n8. **Hundred millions place:**  \n   \\(3 + 8 + 1\\) (carried over) \\(= 12\\)  \n   Write down **12**.\n\nCombining all the results, the final sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1,\\!256,\\!143,\\!595}\n\\]", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1756143595'} 22%|##2       | 112/500 [10:58<39:48,  6.15s/it]
