places, carrying over as needed.\n\nAfter adding all the digits and handling any necessary carries, I will arrive at the final sum.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 666,537,775 and 338,039,615?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n```.\n    666,537,775.\n  + 338,039,615.\n  ==============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 5 = 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 1 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 9\\)  .\n   Write down **9**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 6 = 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1**.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 9\\)  .\n   Write down **9**.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 0 = 6\\)  .\n   Write down **6**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 8 = 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n9. **Hundred millions place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n10. **Billions place:**  .\n    \\(0 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 1\\)  .\n    Write down **1**.\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1004677390'} 26%|##5       | 129/500 [12:38<36:48,  5.95s/it]
