wn **7**.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  \n   \\(2 + 9 = 11\\)  \n   Write down **11**.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\n```\n    217,562,515\n  + 956,081,167\n  ==============\n  1,173,643,682\n```\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{1173643682}\\).", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 217,562,515 and 956,081,167.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 5 + 7 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 1 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 8. I'll write down 8.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 5 + 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nIn the thousands place: 2 + 8 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nFor the ten-thousands place: 6 + 0 plus the carried-over 1 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nIn the hundred-thousands place: 7 + 6 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 1 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nFinally, in the ten-millions place: 2 + 9 equals 11. I'll write down 11.\n\nCombining all the digits, the final sum is 1,173,643,682.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '1173643682', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 217,562,515 and 956,081,167.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 5 + 7 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 1 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 8. I'll write down 8.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 5 + 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nIn the thousands place: 2 + 8 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nFor the ten-thousands place: 6 + 0 plus the 