ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n```.\n    924,581,297.\n  + 671,789,441.\n  ==============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 1 = 8\\).\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 4 = 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 7\\).\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(1 + 9 = 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 8 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 17\\)  .\n   Write down **7** and carry over **1**.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 1 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 6\\).\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 7 = 9\\).\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 6 = 15\\)  .\n   Write down **5** and carry over **1**.\n\n10. **Billions place:**  .\n    The carried over **1** is added as the next digit.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:.\n\n```.\n  1,596,370,738.\n```.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1516370738'} 31%|###       | 154/500 [15:09<37:00,  6.42s/it]
