 down **4**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(9 + 3 = 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the ten millions place.\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  \n   \\(8 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  \n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the hundred millions place.\n\n9. **Hundred millions place:**  \n   \\(8 + 1 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  \n   Write down **10**.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1,044,463,663}\n\\]", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 891,053,187 and 153,410,476.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 7 + 6 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 8 + 7 plus the carried-over 1 equals 16. I'll write down 6 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 1 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nIn the thousands place: 3 + 0 equals 3. I'll write down 3.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 5 + 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 0 + 4 equals 4. I'll write down 4.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 9 + 3 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the ten millions place.\n\nIn the ten millions place: 8 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the hundred millions place.\n\nFinally, in the hundred millions place: 8 + 1 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 10.\n\nCombining all the digits, the final sum is 1,044,463,663.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '1044463663', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 891,053,187 and 153,410,476.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 7 + 6 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the t