arry) \\(= 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(7 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 13\\)  \n   Write down **3** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  \n   \\(6 + 2 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 9\\)  \n   Write down **9**.\n\n9. **Hundred millions place:**  \n   \\(9 + 1 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n10. **Billions place:**  \n    The carried-over **1** is written down.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\n```\n    967,099,234\n  + 125,931,556\n  ==============\n  1,093,030,790\n```\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{1093030790}\\).", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 967,099,234 and 125,931,556.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 4 + 6 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 3 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 9. I'll write down 9.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 2 + 5 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nIn the thousands place: 9 + 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the ten thousands place.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 9 + 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 0 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 7 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the ten millions place.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 6 + 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 9. I'll write down 9.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum of 967,099,234 and 125,931,556 is 1,093,030,790.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '1093030790', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 967,099,234 and 125,931,556.\n\