arry over 1.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 4 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, in the hundred millions place: 8 + 1 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 841,362,456 and 199,915,371?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n```.\n    841,362,456.\n  + 199,915,371.\n  ==============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 1 = 7\\).\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 7 = 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 8\\).\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 5 = 7\\).\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 1 = 7\\).\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 9 = 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Hundred millions place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 1 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n9. **Billions place:**  .\n   The carried-over **1** is written down.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\n```.\n    841,362,456.\n  + 199,915,371.\n  ==============.\n  1,041,277,827.\n```.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1041227827'}
