 place: 5 + 2 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 8 + 0 equals 8. I'll write down 8.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 4 + 7 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the ten millions place.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 7 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 17. I'll write down 17", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 748,521,299 and 937,024,529?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n```.\n    748,521,299.\n  + 937,024,529.\n  ==============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 9 = 18\\)  .\n   Write down **8** and carry over **1**.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 2 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 7\\)  .\n   Write down **7**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(1 + 5 = 6\\)  .\n   Write down **6**.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 2 = 7\\)  .\n   Write down **7**.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 0 = 8\\)  .\n   Write down **8**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 7 = 11\\)  .\n   Write down **1** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 17\\)  .\n   Write down **17**.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\n```.\n    748,521,299.\n  + 937,024,529.\n  ==============.\n  1,685,545,828.\n```.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1685575828'}
