 down 4 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 5 + 7 plus the carried over 1 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 9 + 9 plus the carried over 1 equals 19. I'll write down 9 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place: 4 + 7 plus the carried over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the ten thousands place.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 6 + 5 plus the carried over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 0 + 7 plus the carried over 1 equals 8. I'll write down 8.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 6 + 1 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nFinally, in the hundred millions place: 4 + 6 equals 10. I'll write down 10", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 436,064,957 and 631,579,777?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(7 + 7 = 14\\)  \n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the tens place.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(5 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 13\\)  \n   Write down **3** and carry over **1** to the hundreds place.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(9 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 19\\)  \n   Write down **9** and carry over **1** to the thousands place.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(4 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the ten thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  \n   \\(6 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the hundred thousands place.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  \n   \\(0 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 8\\)  \n   Write down **8**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(6 + 1 = 7\\)  \n   Write down **7**.\n\n8. **Hundred millions place:**  \n   \\(4 + 6 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **10**.\n\nCombining all the results, we ge