ands place: 4 plus 7 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the ten thousands place.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 7 plus 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 2 plus 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 9 plus 4 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the ten millions place.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 6 plus 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 10", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 639274549 and 343672113?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n```.\n    639,274,549.\n  + 343,672,113.\n  ==============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 3 = 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1**.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 1 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 6\\)  .\n   Write down **6**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 2 = 7\\)  .\n   Write down **7**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 7 = 11\\)  .\n   Write down **1** and carry over **1**.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1**.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 6\\)  .\n   Write down **6**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 4 = 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  .\n   Write down **10**.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\n```.\n    639,274,549.\n  + 343,672,113.\n  ==============.\n    982,946,662.\n```.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '988946662'}
