n   \\(6 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  \n   Write down **10**.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\n```\n    639,274,549\n  + 343,672,113\n  ==============\n    982,946,662\n```\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{982946662}\\).", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 639,274,549 and 343,672,113.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the ones place: 9 plus 3 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nThen, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 4 plus 1 plus the carried-over 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 5 plus 2 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nIn the thousands place: 4 plus 7 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the ten thousands place.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 7 plus 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 2 plus 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 9 plus 4 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the ten millions place.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 6 plus 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 10.\n\nCombining all the results, the final sum is 982,946,662.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '982946662', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 639,274,549 and 343,672,113.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the ones place: 9 plus 3 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nThen, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 4 plus 1 plus the carried-over 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 5 plus 2 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nIn the thous