 1\\) (carry) \\(= 17\\)  \n   Write down **7** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  \n   \\(1 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 9\\)  \n   Write down **9**.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{924,\\!767,\\!141}\n\\]", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 127,322,286 and 797,444,855.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 6 + 5 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 8 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 2 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nIn the thousands place: 2 + 4 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 2 + 4 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 3 + 7 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 7 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 17. I'll write down 7 and carry over 1 to the ten millions place.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 1 + 7 plus the carried-over 1 equals 9. I'll write down 9.\n\nCombining all the digits, the sum of 127,322,286 and 797,444,855 is 924,767,141.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '924767141', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 127,322,286 and 797,444,855.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 6 + 5 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 8 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 2 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nIn the thousands place: 2 + 4 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 2 + 4 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 3 + 7 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 7 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 17. I'll write down 7 and carry over 1 to the ten millions place.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 1 + 7 plus the carried-over 1 equals 9. I'll write down 9", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 127,322,286 and 797,444,855?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n```\n    127,322,286\n  + 797,444,855\n  ==============\n```\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(6 + 5 = 11\\)  \n   Write down **1** and carry over **1**.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(8 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  \n   Write down **4** and carry over **1**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(2 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 7\\)  \n   Write down **7**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(2 + 4 = 6\\)  \n   Write down **6**.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  \n   \\(2 + 4 = 6\\)  \n   Write down **6**.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  \n   \\(3 + 7 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(7 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 17\\)  \n   Write down **7** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  \n   \\(1 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 9\\)  \n   Write down **9**.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{924,\\!767,\\!141}\n\\]", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '924767121'}
