ds place:**  \n   \\(2 + 8 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  \n   Write down **1** and carry over **1**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(1 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 6\\)  \n   Write down **6**.\n\n8. **Hundred millions place:**  \n   \\(1 + 9 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n9. **Billions place:**  \n   \\(0 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 1\\)  \n   Write down **1**.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\n```\n    111,280,894\n  + 944,884,438\n  ==============\n    1,056,165,332\n```\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{1056165332}\\).", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 111,280,894 and 944,884,438.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 4 + 8 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 9 + 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 8 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place: 0 + 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 9. I'll write down 9.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 8 + 4 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 2 + 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 1 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nFinally, in the hundred millions place: 1 + 9 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the billions place.\n\nSince there are no higher places, I'll write down the carried-over 1 in the billions place.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum of 111,280,894 and 944,884,438 is 1,056,165,332.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '1056165332', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\