lace.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 4 + 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nIn the thousands place: 0 + 8 equals 8. I'll write down 8.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 6 + 7 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 7 + 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 6 + 7 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the ten millions place.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 1 + 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 5. I'll write down 5", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 167,760,436 and 373,878,287?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n```\n    167,760,436\n  + 373,878,287\n  ==============\n```\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(6 + 7 = 13\\)  \n   Write down **3** and carry over **1**.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(3 + 8 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(4 + 2 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 7\\)  \n   Write down **7**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(0 + 8 = 8\\)  \n   Write down **8**.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  \n   \\(6 + 7 = 13\\)  \n   Write down **3** and carry over **1**.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  \n   \\(7 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  \n   Write down **1** and carry over **1**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(6 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  \n   Write down **4** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  \n   \\(1 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 5\\)  \n   Write down **5**.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{541,\\!638,\\!723}\n\\]", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '541638323'} 71%|#######   | 354/500 [34:54<14:07,  5.81s/it]
