rried over **1**: \\(13 + 1 = 14\\)  \n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the ten-thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  \n   \\(0 + 1 = 1\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(1 + 1 = 2\\)  \n   Write down **2**.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  \n   \\(1 + 9 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the millions place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(0 + 1 = 1\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(1 + 1 = 2\\)  \n   Write down **2**.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  \n   \\(7 + 3 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the hundred-millions place.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  \n   \\(6 + 1 = 7\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(7 + 1 = 8\\)  \n   Write down **8**.\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:\n\n# Answer:\n\\boxed{982,024,751}", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': '\nFirst, I will write down the two numbers to be added: 670,109,857 and 311,914,894.\n\nNext, I will align the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the ones place), I will add each corresponding pair of digits. If the sum of any pair exceeds 9, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will proceed to add the digits in the tens, hundreds, thousands, and all subsequent places, carrying over as needed, until I have added all the digits.\n\nFinally, after completing the addition for all place values, I will arrive at the final sum.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '982024751', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': '\nFirst, I will write down the two numbers to be added: 670,109,857 and 311,914,894.\n\nNext, I will align the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the ones place), I will add each corresponding pair of digits. If the sum of any pair exceeds 9, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will proceed to add the digits in the tens, hundreds, thousands, and all subsequent places, carrying over as needed, until I have added all the digits.\n\nFinally, after completing the addition for all place values, I will arrive at the final sum.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 670,109,857 and 311,914,894?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n```.\n    670,109,857.\n  + 311,914,894.\n  ==============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 4 = 11\\)  .\n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the tens place.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 9 = 14\\)  .\n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(14 + 1 = 15\\)  .\n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the hundreds place.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 8 = 16\\)  .\n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(16 + 1 = 17\\)  .\n   Write down **7** and carry over **1** to the thousands place.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 4 = 13\\)  .\n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(13 + 1 = 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the ten-thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 1 = 1\\)  .\n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(1 + 1 = 2\\)  .\n   Write down **2**.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(1 + 9 = 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the millions place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 1 = 1\\)  .\n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(1 + 1 = 2\\)  .\n   Write down **2**.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 3 = 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the hundred-millions place.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 1 = 7\\)  .\n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(7 + 1 = 8\\)  .\n   Write down **8**.\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '982024711'} 72%|#######1  | 359/500 [35:22<13:22,  5.69s