ry over **1**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(5 + 8 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  \n   Write down **4** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  \n   \\(4 + 2 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 7\\)\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{667,\\!379,\\!447}\n\\]", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 458,987,767 and 208,391,680.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 7 + 0 equals 7.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 6 + 8 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 7 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. Again, I'll write down 4 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the thousands place: 8 + 1 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 9 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 19. I'll write down 9 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 8 + 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1.\n\nNext, the millions place: 5 + 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 4 + 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 7.\n\nCombining all the results, the sum of 458,987,767 and 208,391,680 is 667,379,447.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '667379447', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 458,987,767 and 208,391,680.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 7 + 0 equals 7.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 6 + 8 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 7 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. Again, I'll write down 4 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the thousands place: 8 + 1 plus the 