.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  \n   \\(0 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 7\\)  \n   Write down **7**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(3 + 5 = 8\\)  \n   Write down **8**.\n\n8. **Hundred-millions place:**  \n   \\(1 + 6 = 7\\)  \n   Write down **7**.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{752,\\!711,\\!620}\n\\]", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 137,071,829 and 615,639,791.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 9 + 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 2 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 8 + 7 plus the carried-over 1 equals 16. I'll write down 6 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place: 1 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nFor the ten-thousands place: 7 + 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n\nIn the hundred-thousands place: 0 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 3 + 5 equals 8. I'll write down 8.\n\nFinally, in the hundred-millions place: 1 + 6 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nAfter adding all the digits and handling the carry-over, the final sum is 752,711,620.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '752711620', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 137,071,829 and 615,639,791.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 9 + 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 2 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. I'll write dow