 + 3 = 5  \n  Write down **5**.\n\n- **Millions place:** 1 + 2 = 3  \n  Write down **3**.\n\n- **Ten millions place:** 9 + 3 = 12  \n  Write down **12**.\n\n3. **Combine all the results:**\n\n```\n  191,239,285\n+ 232,332,126\n--------------\n  423,571,411\n```\n\n# Answer:\n\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{423,\\!571,\\!411}\\).", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 191,239,285 and 232,332,126.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 5 + 6 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 8 + 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. Again, I'll write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 2 + 1 plus the carried-over 1 equals 4. I'll write down 4.\n\nIn the thousands place: 9 + 2 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 3 + 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 2 + 3 equals 5. I'll write down 5.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 1 + 2 equals 3. I'll write down 3.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 9 + 3 equals 12. I'll write down 12.\n\nCombining all the results, the final sum is 423,571,411.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '423571411', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 191,239,285 and 232,332,126.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 5 + 6 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 8 + 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. Again, I'll write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 2 + 1 plus the carried-over 1 equals 4. I'll write down 4.\n\nIn the thousands place: 9 + 2 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry ove