gits in the ones place: 3 + 8 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 3 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 9 + 1 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place: 4 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nFor the ten-thousands place: 7 + 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n\nIn the hundred-thousands place: 8 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 0 + 7 plus the carried-over 1 equals 8. I'll write down 8.\n\nFinally, in the ten-millions place: 1 + 4 equals 5. I'll write down 5", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 110,874,933 and 475,219,168?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(3 + 8 = 11\\)  \n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the tens place.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(3 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the hundreds place.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(9 + 1 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  \n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the thousands place.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(4 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  \n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the ten-thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  \n   \\(7 + 2 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the hundred-thousands place.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  \n   \\(8 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  \n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the millions place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(0 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 8\\)  \n   Write down **8**.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  \n   \\(1 + 4 = 5\\)  \n   Write down **5**.\n\nCombining all the digits, the final sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{586,\\!094,\\!101}\n\\]", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '586094107'} 96%|#########6| 481/500 [46:35<01:42,  5.39s/it]
